    "reasoning": "All 16 answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. q-105298: f'(x)=1/x+5\\csc x\\cot x, giving 2/\\pi at \\pi/2. q-1913: the product rule gives -8x^3\\cot x+2x^4\\csc^2 x; the selected choice reverses the order of these terms. q-105314: the product rule gives 5^x\\sec x(\\ln 5+\\tan x). q-70874: f'(\\pi/3)=3/\\pi-3(2/\\sqrt{3})(1/\\sqrt{3})=3/\\pi-2. q-1904: f'(\\pi/6)=-\\pi/3-5(2)(\\sqrt{3})=-\\pi/3-10\\sqrt{3}. For q-113907, q-2161, q-2038, q-113920, q-113936, q-49122, q-71664, and q-71663, differentiating each selected antiderivative reproduces its integrand. q-70359: combining fractions gives numerator 6x-3(2x-1)=3, with x unequal to 0 or 1/2. q-113219: combining over h gives (6h-3)/h=3(2h-1)/h, with h unequal to 0. q-119308: f(2)-1=3 implies f(2)=4, so -f(2)+4=0 and the required point is (2,0). Each field has direct answer evidence in its own worked solution; no grade evidence or earlier solver answer was supplied.",
